#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059460 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059869 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "1b701fb5-7676-5c5f-8a80-b86d2dec0548" :knowledge-point/title "Creating an Exponential Decay Expression From a Decay Rate"}] :question/id #uuid "53dbcc31-f851-5f0f-84e8-ae06de2cc40b" :question/math-academy-id "e-2027" :question/problem "Carlton initially made $\\[math]40\\,000$ annual profit from his business. However, since then, Carlton's annual profit decreased by $12\\%$ every year due to increased competition. To the nearest dollar, what was Carlton's annual profit $4$ years after the increased competition began?" :question/worked-solution "The number $12\\%$ written as a decimal is $0.12$. Therefore, a decrease of $12\\%$ corresponds to multiplication by a factor of\n\n$$\n1-0.12 = 0.88\n$$\n\nTherefore:\n\n- After $1$ year, the annual profit was $40\\,000\\cdot (0.88)$ dollars.\n- After $\\color{blue}2$ years, the annual profit was $40\\,000\\cdot (0.88)^{\\color{blue}2}$ dollars.\n- After $\\color{blue}3$ years, the annual profit was $40\\,000\\cdot (0.88)^{\\color{blue}3}$ dollars.\n- After $\\color{blue}4$ years, the annual profit $40\\,000\\cdot (0.88)^{\\color{blue}4}$ dollars.\n\nFinally, let's evaluate the last expression:\n\n$$\n\\[math]40\\,000\\cdot (0.88)^{4} \\approx \\[/math]23\\,988\n$$\n\nTherefore, Carlton's profit reduced to $\\[math]23\\,988$ after $4$ years."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059461 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059870 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "162c9121-ff80-59f5-85e1-cdeb2729bfc6" :knowledge-point/title "Creating an Exponential Decay Expression From a Decay Factor"}] :question/id #uuid "ebc44409-5898-5525-baed-9c0539defa5e" :question/math-academy-id "e-2028" :question/problem "A radioactive substance decays exponentially such that its mass reduces by $\\dfrac 1 3$ every year. If the mass of the substance was initially $4\\,\\textrm{kg}$, what is the mass of the substance after $6$ years?" :question/worked-solution "If the mass of the substance reduces by\n\n$$\n\\dfrac 1 3\n$$\n\nevery year, then\n\n$$\n\\dfrac 2 3\n$$\n\nof its mass remains every year.\n\nTherefore:\n\n- After $1$ year, the mass is $4\\cdot \\left(\\dfrac 2 3\\right)\\,\\textrm{kg}$.\n- After $\\color{blue}2$ years, the mass is $4\\cdot \\left(\\dfrac 2 3\\right)^{\\color{blue}2}\\,\\textrm{kg}$.\n- After $\\color{blue}3$ years, the mass is $4\\cdot \\left(\\dfrac 2 3\\right)^{\\color{blue}3}\\,\\textrm{kg}$.\n- $\\ldots$\n\nRepeating this pattern, we see that the mass after $\\color{blue}6$ years is\n\n$$\n4\\cdot \\left(\\dfrac 2 3\\right)^{\\color{blue}6}\\,\\textrm{kg}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186060312 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059869 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "1b701fb5-7676-5c5f-8a80-b86d2dec0548" :knowledge-point/title "Creating an Exponential Decay Expression From a Decay Rate"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "84b371cd-cc75-5d93-9194-2dffc2dcb568" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$$5301$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186058495} {:answer/id #uuid "c75be855-b73c-5cdc-ab2f-8e5ac084c33c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$$4902$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186058496} {:answer/id #uuid "e4dcd01a-a785-507c-85f4-84ed9f7d6442" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$$4606$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186058497} {:answer/id #uuid "53d87536-f441-5c2b-b077-7027ed0f357e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$$5067$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186058498} {:answer/id #uuid "71588e64-2ded-50fa-96d7-2d888fef169f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$$4224$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186058499}] :answer-field/id #uuid "5fc3b38a-8bc4-538c-ac92-84c7786b2644" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186058494}] :question/id #uuid "8ea4e5bf-c78f-5012-a71e-1e6ffea002af" :question/math-academy-id "q-61792" :question/problem "A car was purchased for $$7500$ and its value depreciated (decreased) by $15%$ per year. To the nearest dollar, what was the value of the car after $3$ years?"}]}
